<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= typeof lang !== 'undefined' ? lang : 'en' %>" dir="<%= typeof dir !== 'undefined' ? dir : 'ltr' %>">
<head>
<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Terms of Use — Evo Meals' }) %>
<meta name="description" content="The terms that govern use of the Evo Meals platform by parents, students, schools, and catering partners.">
</head>
<body>

<%- include('partials/sitenav', { active: '' }) %>

<section class="hero hero-inner-page">
  <div class="wrap-wide">
    <div class="hero-copy" data-reveal style="max-width:680px;">
      <span class="eyebrow on-dark">Legal</span>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="lede">Last updated 19 September 2026. By creating an account or using Evo Meals, you agree to these terms.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap legal-content">
    <div class="faq-list">

      <div class="faq-item is-open">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="true"><span>Ratification of the Agreement</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>To become a member of the Evo Meals School Meal Program, you'll first complete the registration form and agree to the terms below. By completing that form, or by using our services or ordering a meal through this system, you're agreeing to be bound by these Terms of Use.</p>
          <p>You're responsible for making the arrangements necessary to access the website, and for making sure anyone using your internet connection to access it is aware of, and follows, these terms. By viewing, using, accessing, browsing, or submitting any content on this site, you agree to these Terms of Use as a binding agreement between you and Evo Meals. "You" refers to any person or entity who views, uses, accesses, browses, or submits content to the site. If you don't agree to these terms, please don't use the website.</p>
          <p>We may update these Terms of Use from time to time, without prior notice. Each visit you make to the site is governed by the version in effect at that time, and continuing to use the site after an update means you accept the changes.</p>
          <p>These terms apply to the Evo Meals website and its associated apps on iPhone, iPad, Android, and mobile platforms.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>Description of Services</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>Evo Meals lets registered members book meals online. We provide the way for you to communicate your order to the meal producer and distributor — referred to throughout as the Catering Company, Food Producer, Distributor, Caterer, or Kitchen.</p>
          <p>Our site exists to connect you simply and conveniently with a caterer who prepares, packages, and delivers meals — interactive menus let you build and submit an order in a few clicks.</p>
          <p>Evo Meals is a marketplace for meal ordering and delivery — we don't sell food ourselves, and we don't take part in preparing it. What we provide is the ability to search for, find, and order or subscribe to meals delivered to your school. The catering partner is responsible for complying with Kuwait's local laws and Ministry of Health and Ministry of Education guidelines around food preparation, sale, marketing, and safety.</p>
          <p>It's important to understand that Evo Meals doesn't independently verify a caterer's credentials, claims, ingredients, or kitchen compliance with applicable laws. We'd encourage you to review the information a caterer provides, or reach out to them directly, if you'd like more detail on the quality and reliability of their meals. We don't guarantee that any meal matches exactly what's shown on the site, or that it meets every expectation — our role is the platform connecting you to the people who prepare and deliver your child's food.</p>
          <p>Some caterers may describe a meal outside our "Regular Meal" range as meeting a specific dietary standard — for example, nut-free, egg-free, soya-free, sesame-free, gluten-free, or lactose-free. We don't independently investigate or verify these claims, and we're not liable for any meal or service that doesn't meet your expectations or causes harm.</p>
          <p>You're responsible for making sure your school delivery address is accurate — we're not liable for issues caused by an incorrect address. Food preparation and delivery are entirely the responsibility of the catering partner fulfilling your order. They'll do everything they can to meet the delivery time you're given, but delays can happen for reasons outside their control, and we can't guarantee an exact time. We'll let you know if we become aware of an unexpected delay.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-item">
        <button class="faq-summary" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span>How to Make an Order &amp; How It's Processed</span><span class="plus" aria-hidden="true"></span></button>
        <div class="faq-content">
          <div class="faq-answer"><div class="faq-answer-inner">
          <p>Once you've chosen your order, you'll confirm it by selecting Checkout / Proceed to Pay. Please check your order carefully before this step — once submitted, we're not able to correct input errors. When we receive your order, we'll begin processing it and confirm on-screen that it's been sent successfully to the caterer. If a payment isn't authorized, you'll be returned to the previous page and we won't be able to provide the service for that order.</p>
          <p>Every member has a username and password of their own choosing. Your username is personal to you and won't be shared with another member. Only you know your password, and you can change it any time — keeping it safe is your responsibility, and we're not liable for issues arising from how it's used. We may let you know by email about promotions happening at your child's school that you could benefit from.</p>
          <p>We don't share your information with third parties beyond what's needed to fulfil your order — your name, and your child's and school's information, may be shared with the catering partner preparing and delivering the meal, so your order reaches the right place quickly and correctly. Accessing any part of the service that requires membership means logging in with your username and password.</p>
          <p>By using this site, you're confirming that any personal information you provide is true, accurate, current, and complete, and you agree to let us know if anything changes by updating your profile or contacting us directly. Please don't impersonate another person or use a name you're not authorized to use.</p>
          <p>We ask that each person register only one membership. Registering multiple accounts may result in your membership being closed.</p>
          <p>Keep your password confidential — please don't share it with anyone. You're responsible for activity and orders placed through your account. If you believe someone else knows your password, please contact us right away.</p>
          <p>Please don't use the site for anything unlawful, including sharing unlawful, threatening, or harmful material; sending anything that would breach a law or regulation; interfering with someone else's use of the site; or attempting to gain unauthorized access to the site or its connected systems. We ask that each device be used for one customer account — we may still allow service in other cases, but promotional offers won't apply.</p>
        </div></div>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%- include('partials/sitefoot') %>

</body>
</html>
